    schema:description "Your mission Management of the project development cycle and external service providers such as architects and specialist planners up to the approval planning stage Site assessments and preparation of feasibility studies, area planning and cost estimates for the planning and realization of commercial and residential projects Negotiations with authorities, agencies, urban planners and stakeholders of the urban society Support of urban planning workshop procedures and architectural competitions Supervision of B-plan procedures Management of negotiations for urban development contracts Supervision of neighborhood agreements Processing of internal and external reporting Your profile You have a degree in architecture, civil engineering, real estate management/property management or urban planning or comparable training, e.g. in the field of housing/property management Several years of professional experience in the development of commercial and residential construction projects and building land development Experience in leading project teams Strong communication skills, assertiveness and negotiation skills Legal knowledge of the real estate industry an advantage Why us? Personal development opportunities in a growing group of companies Diverse tasks in a motivated team with creative freedom Flexible and family-friendly working hours Cooperation with pme Familienservice Training and further education opportunities 28 days of vacation plus Christmas Eve and New Year's Eve off work BVG company ticket subsidized by the employer Workplace in a central location with lounge area, table tennis and foosball table Fresh fruit, sweets, coffee, water and more Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
