    schema:datePosted "2026-09-04"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "ArrowStream, a member of Buyers Edge Platform, is a SaaS company transforming how foodservice businesses optimize their supply chains. We're seeking a mid-level Full Stack .NET Engineer to join our Software Development team to build or modernize the customer-facing applications that power this transformation. The ideal candidate is a seasoned full stack engineer who has built, deployed, and maintained enterprise applications, with a demonstrated ability to work across the full software development stack — opinionated but open-minded, with excellent written and verbal English communication skills and the ability to convey complex ideas clearly and professionally to both technical and non-technical audiences. This role involves close collaboration with Product Owners and Business SMEs and facilitating all phases of the software development lifecycle. Hands-on, production-grade LLM-powered solutions experience, as well as cloud/serverless experience, is a plus. Who are we? ArrowStream is reshaping the landscape of supply chain optimization for foodservice businesses. The premier foodservice cloud platform for supply chain intelligence, we've connected over 105,000 restaurant locations to over 1,300 distribution locations, 11,000 manufacturers, and over 275 leading brands. As a Buyers Edge Platform SaaS Solution, ArrowStream customers feel empowered to make informed decisions with our secure cloud-based data management solutions including ArrowStream Central (operators), Crossbow (distributors), and ChainConnect (manufacturers). Not only are we strengthening buying decisions with our industry technology, but we're enforcing pricing accuracy, protecting supply, ensuring quality, and enhancing foodservice partnerships. We are unable to offer work sponsorship for this role. Your impact: Work in an environment focused on continuous delivery and continuous integration. Collaborate closely with the Director of Engineering, other developers, and Product Owners/Business SMEs throughout the SDLC. Actively participate in an agile software development lifecycle, decomposing requirements, discussing and documenting design, effort estimation, and implementation. Participate in the creation of POCs, technical design, and/or requirement documentation. Design, implement, deploy, and support new hosted or cloud-based applications. Track and resolve technical debt and upgrade existing platform components. Troubleshoot and debug issues across the application stack. Develop and maintain SQL Server databases, stored procedures, and data access layers. Adhere to ArrowStream's Coding Standards. Contribute to the knowledge base, wiki, and other ArrowStream resources About you: Bachelors Degree in Computer Science or relevant experience required. 5+ years work, hands-on experience as a Full Stack .NET developer, with experience building web-based applications SQL development experience Strong fundamentals in software design and code craftsmanship Strong work experience using .NET/C# Strong work experience with JavaScript or TypeScript front-end framework Strong SQL Server developer skills Strong experience with source control, DevOps, and CI/CD; git mastery is a plus Work experience with LLM-based application features is a plus Cloud platform and serverless development experience is a plus Not sure you meet every qualification? Studies show that diverse applicants often hesitate to apply unless they check every box. At Buyers Edge Platform, we value authenticity and inclusion—if you're excited about the role, we encourage you to apply. You might be exactly who we’re looking for! What's in this for you: Great benefits from day one. We offer medical, dental, vision, FSA, company-paid life insurance, and more—plus a 401(k) with company match. Grow with us. Enjoy strong training, development, and competitive pay. Work-life balance. Our flexible PTO policy lets you take time when you need it—no accrual required. We welcome all. We are committed to creating a diverse environment and are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to actual or perceived race, color, creed, religion, national origin, ancestry, citizenship status, age, sex or gender (including pregnancy, childbirth and pregnancy-related conditions), gender identity or expression (including transgender status), sexual orientation, marital status, military service and veteran status, physical or mental disability, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state or local laws and ordinances. Originally posted on Himalayas" ;
